{"id": "EUVD-2026-103744", "enisaUuid": "4a889e3b-c5b8-3317-83d1-20b5d3a7a60c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nPCI: of_property: Omit bus properties without a subordinate bus\n\nA bridge (a device with a Type 1 header) may not have a secondary bus\nallocated (pdev->subordinate), e.g., if there are no available bus numbers\nor the bridge secondary/subordinate bus numbers are not writable.\n\nThe dynamic OF helpers of_pci_prop_bus_range() and of_pci_prop_intr_map()\ndereference pdev->subordinate without checking it.  When\nCONFIG_PCI_DYNAMIC_OF_NODES is enabled, this can cause a NULL pointer\ndereference and early boot hang.\n\nGenerate 'bus-range' and 'interrupt-map' properties only when a subordinate\nbus exists.  Keep the node and its remaining properties for bridges without\none.\n\nThe problem was latent since 407d1a51921e (\"PCI: Create device tree node\nfor bridge\"), but wasn't reachable until 1f340724419e (\"PCI: of: Create\ndevice tree PCI host bridge node\"), which appeared in v6.15.  Before\n1f340724419e, of_pci_make_dev_node() returned early because the parent OF\nnode was missing.\n\n[bhelgaas: move pdev->subordinate test to callees, commit log]", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:17:05", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:20:43", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ccd32fa3489cbe86a0b281da4447b4c7eadb3518", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a6d97d10e49ae49026ae13af6c41634fce470a37", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/879c911f77b8a7862aa16079b04efc3fdc5d32ec", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aee774588abd78f75952fd34c3fa461bc46b62c2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8805840aad73df7146778be243a196d48b4f6430"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98504", "GHSA-56f2-rw4q-8x32"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "02c75981-616f-32b1-97bf-88a98f0a0bb5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "1a9d174c-f121-3f64-9f87-30b753f24282", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6"}, {"id": "3ed378b2-7c02-351f-a85a-f3e67b823ae4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "407d1a51921e9f28c1bcec647c2205925bd1fdab <ccd32fa3489cbe86a0b281da4447b4c7eadb3518"}, {"id": "5a9af96c-0778-3617-b444-4e30768828f0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "407d1a51921e9f28c1bcec647c2205925bd1fdab <879c911f77b8a7862aa16079b04efc3fdc5d32ec"}, {"id": "74eeec40-da46-3b8a-9966-91db1bba2d56", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "8271e6b6-15c6-3b60-ba14-4589c76ecc1d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "407d1a51921e9f28c1bcec647c2205925bd1fdab <8805840aad73df7146778be243a196d48b4f6430"}, {"id": "83a8d775-5f27-3beb-80f3-91afe1383dce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "86461588-911a-3cac-aa23-f333cb45a160", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "887b0b23-a47d-3d5f-a7a2-ba73229b779e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "8e830b33-9455-3030-8f96-d829b8eeabe5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "407d1a51921e9f28c1bcec647c2205925bd1fdab <a6d97d10e49ae49026ae13af6c41634fce470a37"}, {"id": "a09e46fb-2ebf-3c32-b7a2-2b1dd12c5c77", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "c805b60e-3b0e-385a-ba04-a57c5945e873", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "407d1a51921e9f28c1bcec647c2205925bd1fdab <aee774588abd78f75952fd34c3fa461bc46b62c2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0b93c971-115e-3a22-baaa-2e57db9d00c3", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}